/*  Operator overloads — `Bind overloading +, given (the lhs is a vec2, the rhs is a vec2): … Done.`

    ★ An overload is a function on an ORDERED pair of operand types: `vec2 * number` and
      `number * vec2` are two declarations. Its C name carries the operator and both type names, so
      no two can meet — and an operator whose two sides make a declared pair calls it, instead of
      doing what the operator would otherwise do.

    ★ An overload writes no result type: it gives what its `Return` gives, worked out from its body
      with its two operands known.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The key an overload is known by among the methods: its operator and both operand types.
    Bind text to overload-key, given (the text operator, the text left-name, the text right-name):
        Return "overload {operator} {left-name} {right-name}".
    Done.

    Bind text to c-overload-name, given (the text operator, the text left-name, the text right-name):
        Return "cfo_{operator}_{cast c-ident on (left-name)}_{cast c-ident on (right-name)}".
    Done.

    /// The name an operand type is declared by — an object's name, or a number, a text, a fact or
    /// bits as itself — or "" for a kind no overload can name.
    Bind text to operand-name, given (the text kind):
        If cast object-of on (kind) is not "", return cast object-of on (kind).
        If cast is-scalar on (kind) or kind is "bits", return kind.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// The kind an operand type name stands for.
    Bind text to operand-kind unto emitter, given (the text type-name):
        If (the entry for type-name in one's objects) is not void, return "object {type-name}".
        Return type-name.
    Done.

    /// The overload a binary expression reaches, or void when its two sides make no declared pair.
    Bind voidable node or failure to overload-for unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        // Most programs declare none, and then no operator need ask what its sides are.
        If (the entry for "%overloads" in one's inferred) is void, return void.
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        If operator is not "Plus" and operator is not "Minus" and operator is not "Star" and operator is not "Slash", return void.
        Define left-name as cast operand-name on (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off).
        Define right-name as cast operand-name on (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off).
        If left-name is "" or right-name is "", return void.
        Return the entry for cast overload-key on (operator, left-name, right-name) in one's methods.
    Done.

    /// The first `Return` anywhere in a body, or void for none.
    Bind voidable node to first-return, given (the node body):
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ReturnStatement", return statement.
            For each part in statement's children, repeat:
                If part's kind is "list" or part's kind is "ConditionArm":
                    Define found as cast first-return on (part).
                    If found is not void, return found.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    /// A writer whose kinds know an overload's two operands.
    Bind emitter to overload-writer unto emitter, given (the node declaration):
        Define writer as cast one's sibling.
        In writer's kinds, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 2)) becomes cast one's operand-kind on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 4))).
        In writer's kinds, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 3)) becomes cast one's operand-kind on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 5))).
        Return writer.
    Done.

    /// What an overload gives: the kind of what its `Return` gives.
    Bind text or failure to overload-gives unto emitter, given (the node declaration):
        Define returned as cast first-return on (cast field-of on (declaration, 6)).
        If returned is void, return a failure (cast not-built on ("an overload that gives nothing back")).
        Define value as cast field-of on (returned, 1).
        If cast is-nothing on (value), return a failure (cast not-built on ("an overload that gives nothing back")).
        If cast is-failure-expression on (value's kind), return a failure (cast not-built on ("an overload that can fail")).
        Define writer as cast one's overload-writer on (declaration).
        Return cast writer's kind-of on (value) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// An overload's head as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-overload-signature unto emitter, given (the node declaration):
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (declaration, 1))'s word.
        Define left-type as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 4)).
        Define right-type as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 5)).
        Define gives as cast one's overload-gives on (declaration) or pass the failure off.
        Define left-c as "{cast c-type on (cast one's operand-kind on (left-type))} {cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 2)))}".
        Define right-c as "{cast c-type on (cast one's operand-kind on (right-type))} {cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 3)))}".
        Return "{cast c-type on (gives)} {cast c-overload-name on (operator, left-type, right-type)}({left-c}, {right-c})".
    Done.

    /// One overload as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-overload unto emitter, given (the node declaration):
        Define writer as cast one's overload-writer on (declaration).
        Cast writer's line on ("int cf_ab = cufet_arena_top; int cf_fo = cufet_alloc_override; (void)cf_ab; (void)cf_fo;").
        In writer's kinds, the entry for "%return" becomes cast one's overload-gives on (declaration) or pass the failure off.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (declaration, 6))'s children, repeat:
            Cast writer's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define signature as cast one's c-overload-signature on (declaration) or pass the failure off.
        Return "{signature} \{\n{writer's body converted to text}\}\n\n".
    Done.

    /// A call of the overload a binary expression reaches, its two sides worked out in order.
    Bind text or failure to c-overload-call unto emitter, given (the node expression, the node declaration):
        Define left-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define right-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Define sides as a series of text with (left-c, right-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 3)), sides).
        Define called as cast c-overload-name on ((cast field-of on (declaration, 1))'s word,
            cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 4)), cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 5))).
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, "{called}({item 1 of sides}, {item 2 of sides})").
    Done.
Done.
